    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0466" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.W./10–1444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador to the Greek Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-14T12:00:00+03:00">October 14,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek Series 365. The Greek Minister to Egypt<anchor n="6" xml:id="d388-f1"/> has
                    notified me verbally that last Wednesday afternoon his colleague in Moscow was
                    summoned by Mr. Molotoff and informed that Bulgarian troops have been ordered to
                    evacuate Greek territory completely, the movement to be completed in 15 days.
                    Pappas added with evident relief and satisfaction that the whole tone of Mr.
                    Molotoff’s conversation with the Greek representative was “more friendly and
                    easy” than has been the case previously.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Caserta as No. 96 and to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d388-f1" n="6" xml:id="d388-f1-content">
